BIOLOGICAL INTERPRETATION:
  1. UL23 Thymidine Kinase:
     Corrected BLOSUM62 radicalness achieves 0.6380 +/- 0.0690 under contiguous-block,
     with every individual block exceeding 0.55 (B0=0.557, B1=0.575, B2=0.660, B3=0.683, B4=0.715).
     This confirms that for missense variants in UL23, amino acid radicalness alone provides
     a consistent, non-trivial predictive signal that generalizes across spatial regions.
  2. UL30 DNA Polymerase:
     Corrected BLOSUM62 radicalness collapses completely under contiguous-block holdout:
     UL30-ACV is 0.5494 +/- 0.2496 and UL30-FOS is 0.5074 +/- 0.2997 (both at chance).
     Simple amino acid radicalness has zero predictive power for polymerase resistance;
     only structural and evolutionary representations (PLMs, MSA) capture UL30 resistance.